<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well Mr \'85\'92 Johnny squinted at the card. \'91Damage eat us?\'92 He shifted his squint to Chilo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Close enough.\'92 Chilo shrugged. \'91My father\'92s name. It\'92s Greek.\'92 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, of course it is,\'92 Johnny said, recovering some of his know-it-all demeanour. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo, assessing the greetings over, presumed to take the seat opposite Johnny. \'91Excuse me, waiter. Coffee please.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Without the gold leaf,\'92 Johnny added, believing this vagabond would stiff him for paying the bill. A little more alert, he scrutinised the old man: long beard, crazed skin, deep eyes, a cat\'92s grin that dripped of fang and mischief. \'91Wait \'85\'92 Johnny assembled some mental pieces. \'91You\'92re one of those lunatics who accosted Sarah \'85 at the 
\f2\i Memphis Bar
