\f2\i  Mafia 
\f1\i0 Bar,\'92 Chilo corrected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Is that supposed to make it better?\'92 Johnny recalled the obscene proposition these clowns had made Sarah: 
\f2\i if it isn\'92t too much trouble, could we get you pregnant?
\f1\i0  But Johnny\'92s thought raced to an even more heinous offence. \'91You and your friends almost got me killed.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I think you will find it was the PAPER agents who were the aggressors that night, and it was one of my colleagues who diffused the situation.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny didn\'92t recall it that way; he was sure it was himself who brokered a stand-off that night, which gave Sarah enough time to flee, but he admitted to himself things were hazy after an Elvi waitress had assaulted him. \'91So where\'92s the rest of your minstrel troupe then?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91My esteemed colleagues are unawares of my whereabouts,\'92 Chilo said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny sensed he was being sly. \'91What\'92s this about?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo patted the linen table and popped his lips a couple of times while he assembled his thoughts. \'91I understand you had a mishap recently.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny became steel, the way he knew he always could. \'91I\'92ve had no 
\f2\i mishaps
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh, I\'92d call blowing up a Shakti Research facility a mishap.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How do you know about that?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo sat back, easing into his rehearsed agenda. \'91There were deaths.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny held his breath and stared Chilo. The coffee arrived. Chilo slurped it, and earned disapproving murmurs from nearby tables.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Go on,\'92 Johnny said, defying Chilo to make matters worse.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You spun a Gyges disc.\'92 He made it worse. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny felt his lungs turn to ice. His back prickled like metal fibres were growing out of it. Chilo let him sit in terror for as long as he dared. \'91Fear not, young Stoat. I\'92ve come to help you.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Johnny scoffed. \'91How can you help me?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91When you spin a Gyges disc you create an astronomically complex environment. The laws of physics\'85\'92 Chilo studied Johnny and decided to dumb it down. \'91What you created in your lab was something like a very very \'85 very small black hole.\'92
